`-revert=safedefault` builds code written for upstream D

The switch makes unannotated functions `@system` (upstream's default), for
code bases written for upstream D. The Destiny compiler builds its own sources
with it, and so do Destiny's dub and serve-destiny.

$(UL
$(LI The libraries shipped with the compiler (druntime and Fate) keep the
`@safe` default, since they are prebuilt with it and their mangled names must
match.)
$(LI Code a Fate template generates for a module (for example the methods
`std.typecons.AutoImplement` writes) follows that module's default.)
$(LI An override without its own safety attribute, of a method that is
`@safe` only by Destiny's default (`Object.toString`, `opEquals`, `opCmp`,
`toHash`), is not checked as `@safe` under the switch. `@safe` code can still
call it through `Object`.)
$(LI `build.d` passes the switch automatically when the host compiler is
Destiny.)
)
